  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 6aadde69f514c7545ac8b7ebefed8893, type: 3}
  m_Name: FactsData_Room3_Isolated
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  facts:
  - An isolated system exchanges NEITHER matter nor energy with its surroundings.
  - A perfect thermos flask is the closest real-world example of an isolated system.
  - "Truly isolated systems don't exist in nature \u2014 they are theoretical ideals."
  - In an isolated system, total energy always remains constant.
  - The universe itself is considered the only true isolated system.
